# FigDown — figures as text. Spec: https://github.com/FigDown/figdown

# Classic teaching FSM: subway turnstile (Hopcroft/Ullman-style example).
# Interim spelling: figdown 0.1 block (portable). Planned genre: statechart
# (decisions/registry.md) — not registered in the engine yet.
#
# Authoring style: short canvas labels; multi-line human notes as # lines
# (Markdown-like editing — do not pack the whole story into mid labels).
figdown 0.1 block
title "Turnstile statechart (classic FSM)"

class mode "A mode of the turnstile mechanism" fill=#e0e7ff

# ── states ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
node locked "LOCKED" class=mode
# Barrier locked. Coin is accepted; pushing the arm does nothing useful.

node unlocked "UNLOCKED" class=mode
# Barrier free for one passage. A second coin is kept (or ignored);
# push returns the machine to LOCKED.

# ── transitions ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
edge locked -[coin]-> unlocked
# trigger: coin
# effect: unlock barrier (one fare)

edge unlocked -[push]-> locked
# trigger: push (person passes)
# effect: relock barrier

edge locked -[push]-> locked
# trigger: push while locked
# effect: none (stay locked) — self-loop

edge unlocked -[coin]-> unlocked
# trigger: extra coin while unlocked
# effect: none / farebox keeps coin — self-loop

flow right
rank locked,unlocked
